# Aang, the Last Airbender, cast on turn 1 with Plains and three Moxen, airbends up to one other nonland permanent: Bot1 picks his
# own Mox Jet, already tapped for the mana (a controller's own permanent is a fine target), and it is exiled. On turn 3 Bot1
# casts Airbending Lesson (a Lesson spell: "Whenever you cast a Lesson spell, Aang gains lifelink until end of turn") on Bot2's
# Ornithopter, so Aang attacks with lifelink and Bot1 gains 3 (23), Bot2 loses 3 (17). On turn 5 Bot1 casts only an Ornithopter,
# not a Lesson, and Aang's second attack gains nothing: lifelink ended with turn 3 and was not given again (Bot1 stays at 23, Bot2 14).

